+# BUG-260917-2fwf8e results
+
+Status: ready for review; candidate intentionally uncommitted for the Story
+handoff snapshot.
+
+## Outcome
+
+`internal/fencing.Authorize` now preserves refresh-policy validation but defers
+only the lapsed-grant refusal until after ownership direction. A remote winner
+with a lapsed local grant therefore returns the existing `remote_owner` park
+with literal `not_owner`, rather than `lease_conflict`. `axpane.Decide` can
+then emit `attach_remote` or `takeover_offer` for an interactive caller and
+`parked` for a non-interactive caller. A local lapsed grant remains literal
+`lease_conflict`; a remote unusable policy remains literal
+`invalid_arguments`.
+
+No lease-chain implementation or park vocabulary changed.
+
+## Probe 10 before/after
+
+Source archive:
+`TASK-260830-1geqhj_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz`, SHA-256
+`9f473449f33fda2be591f23396da2b9b9b995ba18708b02afdff7a550e840ef4`.
+
+| Production surface | Before | After |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Direct `fencing.Authorize` | Refused `lease_conflict`; cause said the fencing grant lapsed | Parked `remote_owner` under the winning lease; cause `not_owner` |
+| `axpane.Decide`, interactive + attach admitted | `refused / lease_conflict` | `attach_remote / remote_owner` |
+| `axpane.Decide`, interactive + attach not admitted | `refused / lease_conflict` | `takeover_offer / remote_owner` |
+| `axpane.Decide`, non-interactive | `refused / lease_conflict` | `parked / remote_owner` |
+
+Evidence logs:
+
+- Before direct: `runs/probe10-authorize-before.log`
+- After direct: `runs/probe10-authorize-after.log`
+- Before composed: `runs/probe10-decide-before.log`
+- After composed: `runs/probe10-decide-after.log`
+
+The archived probe source itself references the removed `Realm.AttestedServer`
+field and cannot compile unchanged on the current tree. The current minimal
+probe and the committed direct regression reproduce the same vector; this API
+drift is recorded as a bound rather than inferred away.
+
+## Named production tests
+
+- `internal/fencing/authorize_order_test.go`
+  - `TestAuthorizeRemoteInteractiveOwnerLapsedGrantUsesRemoteOfferArm`
+    calls `Authorize` directly and asserts literal `remote_owner`,
+    `not_owner`, and absence of `lease_conflict`.
+  - `TestAuthorizeArmOrderingNeighbourVectors` drives live local,
+    remote/non-interactive, and local/lapsed vectors directly.
+  - `TestAuthorizeRemoteOwnerInvalidPolicyRemainsInvalidArguments` pins the
+    preserved remote invalid-policy refusal.
+- `internal/axpane/decide_test.go`
+  - `TestDecideLapsedRemoteOwnerOffersOrParksByInteractiveContext` drives the
+    composed `Decide` entry for attach, takeover, and noninteractive park.
+- `internal/terminstance/fencing_grantless_test.go`
+  - Updated old expiry-first expectations to the correct remote-owner park/no
+    transition; hard grant-precondition refusals still fence as before.
+
+Coverage ratio for the task behavior: 4 of 4 direct fencing vectors driven;
+3 of 3 wrapper-context outcomes driven; 1 of 1 arm-order mutant row killed.
+The production call sites and explicit bounds are in
+`BUG-260917-2fwf8e_conformance-matrix.md` and
+`internal/fencing/TRACEABILITY.md`.
+
+## Per-test fencing diff
+
+Baseline:
+`runs/fencing-before.jsonl` / `runs/fencing-before-tests.sorted.tsv` — 310
+PASS rows.
+
+After:
+`runs/fencing-after-v2.jsonl` / `runs/fencing-after-tests.sorted.tsv` — 316
+PASS rows.
+
+Normalized diff:
+`runs/fencing-outcome-diff-v2.sorted.patch`.
+
+Only six new PASS rows appear: the arm-order neighbor test and its three
+subtests, the direct remote-lapsed test, and the remote-invalid-policy test.
+No pre-existing per-test outcome changed or moved across a refusal arm.
+
+## Mutant evidence
+
+Final full harness:
+`runs/mutants-full-v3/` (rerun after the final literal-token assertion
+strengthening).
+
+- 31 narrowing `N-` mutants: all KILLED with real exit 1.
+- `T-census-alias`: KILLED while the behavioral suite runs, preserving the
+  searched token.
+- `C-harmless-comment`: SURVIVED control.
+- `C-not-applied`: NOT_APPLIED control.
+- `C-compile-failure`: `COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE`, exit 1.
+- `N-arm-order-expiry-before-direction`: KILLED the direct regression.
+- Harness ran with `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; no `__pycache__` or `.pyc`
+  files were found.
+
+## Validation
+
+The configured 30-command validation list was run with exit 0. Logs and
+per-command exit files are under `runs/`:
+
+- `01-final-gofmt.log` through `06-final-go-test-cover.log`: formatting,
+  build, vet, verbose suite, race suite with the configured 25-minute timeout,
+  and coverage.
+- `07`–`23`: all configured fuzz targets, 100 executions each, one worker.
+- `24-tracecheck.log`, `25-cataloggen-check.log`, `26-linux-build.log`,
+  `27-windows-build.log`, `28-json-parse.log`,
+  `29-task-board-validate.log`, and `30-git-diff-check.log`.
+- Extra producer-required `windows-vet.log`: exit 0.
+- Focused final package run after literal-token assertion strengthening:
+  `final-relevant-after-literal-tests.log`: `internal/fencing`,
+  `internal/axpane`, and `internal/terminstance` all exit 0.
+
+The first post-reorder full/race attempt failed on the old
+`terminstance` expiry-first assertions. Those tests were updated to the new
+specified arm ordering; final verbose, race, and coverage runs then passed.
+`task-board validate` exited 0, with its existing ledger notice of 180 issues
+and 2696/2696 mirrored rows; no board files were edited.
+
+## Scope/bounds
+
+- `internal/traceability` was not edited.
+- `sessrepo.CheckFencingExpiry` remains the expiry owner.
+- No lease append, tuple, chain, or park vocabulary implementation changed.
+- No public `ax` CLI surface is claimed; the offer path is measured through
+  the existing `axpane.Decide` production entry.
+- The candidate remains uncommitted on
+  `task-board/story/STORY-260917-kf9g1h` for handoff.
