+| Arm ordering is pinned and swap is shipped | `fencing.Authorize` | `N-arm-order-expiry-before-direction` in `internal/fencing/testdata/mutate.py` | 1 of 1 arm-order rows: the isolated expiry-first swap exits 1 and kills the direct regression. |
+| Previously reported vector plus neighbours | `fencing.Authorize`; `axpane.Decide` | `TestAuthorizeArmOrderingNeighbourVectors/{live_local_grant,remote_noninteractive_owner,local_owner_lapsed_grant}`; composed context test | 4 of 4 direct vectors driven: live local → authorized; remote noninteractive → `remote_owner`; local lapsed → `lease_conflict`; reported remote lapsed → offer park. 3 of 3 wrapper contexts driven: attach, takeover, noninteractive park. |
+| Other refusal placement remains stable | `fencing.Authorize` | `TestAuthorizeRemoteOwnerInvalidPolicyRemainsInvalidArguments`; existing `TestAuthorizeRefusesExpiredGrant` | Remote unusable policy remains literal `invalid_arguments`; local lapsed remains literal `lease_conflict`; policy validity is not moved behind direction. |
+| Existing arm outcomes do not silently move | `internal/fencing` package entry points | `fencing-before.jsonl`, `fencing-after-v2.jsonl`, `fencing-outcome-diff-v2.sorted.patch` | 310 baseline PASS rows vs 316 final PASS rows; the normalized diff contains only six added named rows from this leaf and no changed existing outcome. |
