+# BUG-260917-2fwf8e conformance matrix
+
+Authority: `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`, §4.2 after-restore sequence,
+step 4. The assigned implementation scope is the arm ordering in
+`internal/fencing.Authorize`; the lease chain remains owned by `sessrepo` and
+the `session.parked` vocabulary remains owned by `internal/fencing`.
+
+## Acceptance rows
+
+| Row | Production call site | Named test/evidence | Result and ratio |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Remote interactive owner with a lapsed local grant reaches the offer path | `fencing.Authorize(OperationRestore, ...)`, then `axpane.Decide` | `TestAuthorizeRemoteInteractiveOwnerLapsedGrantUsesRemoteOfferArm`; `TestDecideLapsedRemoteOwnerOffersOrParksByInteractiveContext/interactive_attach`; `/interactive_takeover` | 1 of 1 reported vector: direct `remote_owner` park with literal `not_owner`, never literal `lease_conflict`; composed actions are literal `attach_remote` and `takeover_offer`. |
+| Arm ordering is pinned and swap is shipped | `fencing.Authorize` | `N-arm-order-expiry-before-direction` in `internal/fencing/testdata/mutate.py` | 1 of 1 arm-order rows: the isolated expiry-first swap exits 1 and kills the direct regression. |
+| Previously reported vector plus neighbours | `fencing.Authorize`; `axpane.Decide` | `TestAuthorizeArmOrderingNeighbourVectors/{live_local_grant,remote_noninteractive_owner,local_owner_lapsed_grant}`; composed context test | 4 of 4 direct vectors driven: live local → authorized; remote noninteractive → `remote_owner`; local lapsed → `lease_conflict`; reported remote lapsed → offer park. 3 of 3 wrapper contexts driven: attach, takeover, noninteractive park. |
+| Other refusal placement remains stable | `fencing.Authorize` | `TestAuthorizeRemoteOwnerInvalidPolicyRemainsInvalidArguments`; existing `TestAuthorizeRefusesExpiredGrant` | Remote unusable policy remains literal `invalid_arguments`; local lapsed remains literal `lease_conflict`; policy validity is not moved behind direction. |
+| Existing arm outcomes do not silently move | `internal/fencing` package entry points | `fencing-before.jsonl`, `fencing-after-v2.jsonl`, `fencing-outcome-diff-v2.sorted.patch` | 310 baseline PASS rows vs 316 final PASS rows; the normalized diff contains only six added named rows from this leaf and no changed existing outcome. |
+
+## Reviewer probe 10
+
+Input was reproduced from the review archive
+`TASK-260830-1geqhj_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz` (SHA-256
+`9f473449f33fda2be591f23396da2b9b9b995ba18708b02afdff7a550e840ef4`).
+
+| Surface | Before fix | After fix |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Direct `Authorize` | `action=refused class=lease_conflict`; `fencing grant ... lapsed` | `park=remote_owner` under the winning lease; `cause=not_owner` |
+| Composed `Decide`, interactive + attach admitted | `action=refused class=lease_conflict` | `action=attach_remote`, `reason=remote_owner` |
+| Composed `Decide`, interactive + attach not admitted | `action=refused class=lease_conflict` | `action=takeover_offer`, `reason=remote_owner` |
+| Composed `Decide`, non-interactive | `action=refused class=lease_conflict` | `action=parked`, `reason=remote_owner` |
+
+The archived `zz_review_probe_test.go` could not compile unchanged against the
+current tree because it refers to the removed `Realm.AttestedServer` field.
+That is an explicit reproduction bound, not an inferred absence. The current
+minimal probe and the committed direct regression use the same lapsed-grant /
+remote-winner vector and produced the before/after logs above.
+
+## Negative and mutant evidence
+
+The negative tests assert literal specification tokens (`remote_owner`,
+`not_owner`, `lease_conflict`, `invalid_arguments`, `attach_remote`,
+`takeover_offer`, and `parked`) at the production entry or its named composed
+caller. The final full `mutate.py` run is in `runs/mutants-full-v3`:
+
+- 31 `N-` narrowing mutants: KILLED with real subprocess exit 1.
+- 1 `T-census-alias` token-preserving source-text mutant: KILLED while the
+  behavioral suite runs.
+- `C-harmless-comment`: SURVIVED as the harmless control.
+- `C-not-applied`: NOT_APPLIED as the neutral control.
+- `C-compile-failure`: classified `COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE`, exit 1.
+- The arm-order row is explicitly labelled
+  `N-arm-order-expiry-before-direction`; its raw log and JSON row are present.
+- `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` was used; no `__pycache__` or `.pyc` files were
+  present in the evidence directory.
+
+## Scope and validation
+
+The production delta is the saved expiry result plus ownership-direction
+precedence in `internal/fencing/gate.go`. `sessrepo.CheckFencingExpiry` is
+still the sole expiry owner. No lease-chain or park-vocabulary production
+change was made. `internal/traceability` was not edited. The only outside
+package changes are the required `terminstance` test/comment updates that
+remove the old expiry-first expectation from an existing composed test.
+
+The configured validation list from `task-board.config.json` was run with
+exit 0 for commands 1–30. Logs are in `runs/` with matching `.rc` files:
+
+- gofmt, build, vet, full verbose tests, race (`-timeout 25m`), and full
+  coverage all passed; `internal/fencing` coverage was 97.9%.
+- fuzz commands 7–23 all completed 100x with `parallel=1`.
+- tracecheck passed (`contracts=64`, `acceptance_cases=152`, `clauses_discharged=70/574`); catalog check, Linux/Windows builds, Windows vet, JSON parsing, board validation, and `git diff --check` passed.
+- The first full/race run after the production reorder failed only on the
+  pre-existing `terminstance` expectations for expiry-first remote lapsed
+  grants. Those assertions were updated to the new `remote_owner` behavior,
+  and the final full verbose/race/coverage runs passed.
+- `task-board validate` returned exit 0 while printing its existing ledger
+  notice (`180 issue(s) found`, `2696/2696 checked rows mirrored`); no board
+  files were edited.
+
+The candidate is intentionally uncommitted in the managed Story worktree;
+the handoff snapshot owns commit creation.
