+## 2026-09-21
+
+### BUG-260917-2fwf8e — fencing direction must beat lapsed-grant refusal
+
+- SCOPE: `internal/fencing.Authorize` arm precedence only. `sessrepo.CheckFencingExpiry` remains the expiry owner; no lease-chain code or Section 5.2 park vocabulary changed. The old `terminstance` grantless assertions that encoded expiry-first behavior were updated to expect the existing literal `remote_owner` park for a remote lapsed grant, with no stale-fence transition.
+- REPRO: reviewer archive `TASK-260830-1geqhj_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz`, SHA-256 `9f473449f33fda2be591f23396da2b9b9b995ba18708b02afdff7a550e840ef4`, probe 10 from `RUN-260917-3934e0`. Before: direct `Authorize(OperationRestore, ...)` returned literal `lease_conflict`; composed `axpane.Decide` returned `refused/lease_conflict` for attach, takeover, and noninteractive park. The archived probe file itself no longer compiles on this tree because it references removed `Realm.AttestedServer`; a minimal current-tree probe and the committed direct test reproduced the vector instead (bounded, recorded in results).
