LOGBOOK.md:1994:- ROOT CAUSE: every vocabulary had a "refuses a value outside the vocabulary" negative, which proves the gate is REACHABLE, not that the admitted set is the DECLARED set. Coverage cannot separate the two: a widened gate still executes its refusal for whichever outside value the test picked. This is the same shape as the bounds finding one round earlier — an obligation that does not carry the literal cannot fail when the literal moves.
LOGBOOK.md:1998:- SCOPE, measured and disclosed rather than fixed: the same two derived sweeps were pointed at `canonical.go` and `closed_shapes.go`, the preceding leaves, because "we did not look" and "there is nothing there" are different facts. 262 mutants, 200 killed, 12 not compilable, **50 survivors**. All 18 guard-deletion survivors are equivalent mutants already declared in `unreachableRefusalSites` with a subsuming refusal and a named proving test, matched return-by-return. The other **32 are real one-directional proofs** in the preceding leaves — an equality coupling with a counterpart on one lexical side only, and a strictly-sorted list proven by reversal but never by a duplicate. Both shapes were claimed closed for `core_records.go` in that revision. The full per-survivor list, with what each mutant silently admits, ships as `TASK-260830-1tax26_rev4-preceding-leaf-survivors.md`; the natural owner is the sibling `TASK-260830-uqnwmi`, whose deliverable is exactly this conformance-test class.
LOGBOOK.md:1999:- CORRECTION (2026-09-02, revision 6): "Both shapes are closed for `core_records.go` in this revision" does not reproduce and is corrected above. The revision-4 grammar rewrote comparison OPERATORS, which cannot express either of the two shapes review then found in `core_records.go`: a boolean-valued `!=` has no operator to rewrite, only a boolean identity to split into `a && !b` / `!a && b`; and `epoch != 1` narrowed to `epoch > 1` is an equivalent mutant, so the operator sweep provably could not reach the `epoch >= 3` narrowing that admitted an epoch-2 lease with a null predecessor. The honest revision-4 claim is: the one-directional EQUALITY-COUPLING shape the operator grammar could express was closed for `core_records.go`; the boolean-identity and literal-boundary shapes were never swept there. Both are closed in revision 6 by standing derived gates, not by a sweep.
